  <data name="BotDaycareEgg_Help" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Deposit two Pokemon that can breed at the Day-Care (Solaceon Town in Diamond/Pearl/Platinum, Route 34 in HeartGold/SoulSilver; the Day-Care Man must not have an egg waiting), stand on a straight path without trainers or tall grass, facing the way to walk, then press Start. The bot walks until just before the next egg check, saves a state there and reloads it with new random numbers until the egg the Day-Care Man gets is shiny. It then stops: walk to the Day-Care Man and take the egg (its IVs are decided when you take it), and save in the game.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BotDaycareEgg_NeedTwo" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Deposit two Pokemon that can breed at the Day-Care first.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BotDaycareEgg_EggWaiting" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Day-Care Man already has an egg: take it (or refuse it) before starting.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BotDaycareEgg_ShinyFound" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Shiny egg! Walk to the Day-Care Man and take it, then save in the game.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BotDaycareEgg_NoEgg" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No egg after {0} tries: these two Pokemon can't breed together.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BotDaycareEgg_HelpGen5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Black/White/Black 2/White 2 (Day-Care on Route 3) and Omega Ruby/Alpha Sapphire (Route 117): the egg is only decided when you take it. Deposit two Pokemon that can breed and walk until the Day-Care Man (outside, by the door) has an egg for you. Make room in your party, stand in front of him facing him, then press Start. The bot saves a state there, takes the egg and reloads with new random numbers until the egg is shiny. It then stops with the shiny egg in your party: save in the game.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BotDaycareEgg_NoEggYet" xml:space="preserve">
